        <p>------ - FIRE GRATES. If you want a row grate oar larg and varied stock will interest you.—J. S. GARLAND Bridge St., Warrington.—Advt. Catholic Charity Bail. The second annual Catholic Charity Ball was held at the Lion Hotel on Wednesday evening and, like its predecessor, proved most successful and enjoyable. Although the weather was as unfavourable as possible, the attendance reached the satisfactory number of 110 The Mayor and Mayoress (Councillor Dr. and Miss seph), were present. The ball ro-m had been attractively decorated by Mr. 11,11ph Johnson and its bright and p'cur-e-ijue appearance was generally com- mented upon. Mr. W. P. Bayley 's well-known band submitted a clo,ice programme of 21 dances. Mr. C. H. Wells was an efficient MC. and the duties of stewards were admirably discharged by Messrs. E. A. Connor (chairman of committee), 0. Toole, R. H. Lowe, M. Cunningham, J. Hind, J. Cunningham and H. Dolan. Mr. T. J. Houghton, ton. secretary, is to be complimented upon the excellence of the arrange- ments. The catering of Mr. John Lee gave every jEta tisfaction.</p>
        <p>tlia members interested). Th 3 six portrait studies that won the first priz3 in that section are worthy of their place, and so are the architectural series. A set of 'slides illuvrating the Scotch sung " Cuddle doen," are a charming rendering of sleeping (and wide- awake) children, and the feeding of a young cuckoo by a song thrush was another subj-ct highly praised. The direct colour photographs ara still wanting in many respects' but one of primroses artificially stained a delicate and natural yellow was perhaps awarded the heartiest applause of the evening. The new light for the lantern, obtained at the hands of Mr. H. Smith, chemist, is admirable in every way, as much in its simplicity as in its brilliance. CUTLERY, Rodgers celebrated knives and forks, &amp;c 3 —Agent, J. S. GARLAND, Ironmonger, Bridg3 Warrington.—Advt. Foresters' Quarterly Meeting. The Warrington District of the Ancient Order of Foresteis held their 200th quarterly meeting at the Hotn3 Inn, Farnworth, near Widnes, on Siturday last. The district board consisted of the following :—Bros. G W R Baines D.C.R., T Roden S.D C 8., S B Healey</p>
