        <p>MANX STEAMER'S EXPERIENCE.</p>
        <p>When the s.s. Douglas from Liverpool arrived at Douglas at'a quarter to five on Wednesday the sea was breaking over the pier and breakwater, and it was impossible to land the passengers. Signals were fired, and Captain Tanner steamed to sea again, and remained beating off the port for four hours. At a quarter to ten there was enough water to run straight into tl e old harbour, and the boat was then brought alongside the old pier. There were very few passengers on board, but they had a trying experience.</p>
