      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-01-20_WidnesExaminer_art0084" n="art0084">
        <head>rich</head>
        <p>rich</p>
        <p>S</p>
        <p>L/G/01/</p>
        <p>Warrington Parish Church. At the Liverpool Consistory Court on Wednesday consent was given to the Rev. Frederic William Willis M.A. (rector), and Messrs. James Grice Craik and Edward Isherwood (wardens), of St. Elphin's Church, Warrington, to take down the present vestry and erect a larger one, and to alter the choir stalls and the seats in rear by removing them to feet in a westerly direc- tion. The estimated cost will be defrayed by voluntary contributions. A faculty was further granted confirm- ing the placing of a cross,two vases,and two candlesticks all of brass, up m a re-table abo vs the communion table in the church, and also upon the re-table in the Boteler Chapel.</p>
        <p>U</p>
