      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-01-20_WidnesExaminer_art0091" n="art0091">
        <head>TO CALCUTTA.</head>
        <p>TO CALCUTTA.</p>
        <p>THE KING'S VISIT</p>
        <p>.. One of the most brilliant and splendid episodes of their Majesties' visit to India way/ we Pageant of India, held on the Calcutta Maidan. It had a character entirely its own, being Indian in every detail. More than 50 elephants, 35 camels, hundreds of horses, ancient yeomanry and retainers, and many elaborate State cars were included in tha procession. Our photograph shows some of the magnificently draped elephants bearing gold and silver howdahs.</p>
        <p>"tW FRENCH PREMIER. M. Potncare, has refused the Premiership on two previous occasions. A man of great versatility, the new Premier is well versed in art, science, literature and politics. He Is_ 51 years of age, and has twice been 4`Unister of Finance.</p>
        <p>S. SEDDON. Seddon, whose husband has for weeks been in custody on a charge</p>
        <p>murdering a wealthy lodger, Miss Eliza Barrow, at Tollington Park, North London, administering arsenic, has been arrested :onnection with the case.</p>
        <p>SPLENDOURS OF THE CALCUTTA PAGEANT. a We produce above the finest of the wonderful elephant cars that took part in the fireat Pageant of India. This vehicle, said to be the heaviest in the world, is richly decorated in gold and silver, and the elephants wear beaten silver head-dress and OrgeOns drapings.</p>
