      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-01-20_WidnesExaminer_art0092" n="art0092">
        <head>WARRINGTON COMMERCIAL</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON COMMERCIAL</p>
        <p>TRAVELLERS.</p>
        <p>Annual Meeting. The fti Mil annual meeting of the Warrington branch. Clf th tio e United Kingdom Commercial Travellers, Associa 41111.11 iwtte held at the Lion Hotel on Saturday, Mr. mOid Mercer (the retiring chairman), presiding. W. L. WALRen, as delegate,lgave his report of the Otoorih, , West Federation meeting held at Birkenhead, on se,er 21 at. BEDI4 eral new members were enrolled and the Hos. tisno-,TARY (111 r. W. G. Hayes), submitted his annual tk;ti giving an interesting account of the working of tten„,e4rleb during the past year. He referred to the poiX" Society in connection with the Association, tho-"leg out the advantages to members and urging PI to avail themselves of the benefits to be obtained Hing the Society. IrOpori "s.N. TREASURER (Tr. W. P. Ashton) read his Past Notwithstanding some heavy payments of the ktt "ear the balance sheet was considered very satis- T, was duly adopted on the motion of Mr. J. 11;cio,WLEs, seconded by Mr. H. L TAYLOR. n'• ". P. RYLANDS having signified his acceptance pisifilee for another year, wss unanimously Fe-elected tsstnbeueret of the branch, Much to the satisfaction of the The a' C4o,oll,owing were elected vice-presidents :—Messrs. V.. 0 P Caldwell, A If Crosfield, John Dolan, Grencillor Alf enell and John Lee ; hon. vice-presidents, Messrs. J T Locker, Messrs J Fulton-Smith, Henry Knowles, H Mercer, E Warren, and W L bon. solicitor, Mr T S Steel. ktitl r' W' Gt- Hayes was elected chairman for the year 1,114_ r• Frank Plumpton vice-chairman. 41,thtr: Allen was appointed secretary, and Mr. W P. treo`dal Who was the only nominee for the office of this "tir6ri was unanimously re-elected and thanked for dot, efficient manner in which he had carried out the tier° ~,for several years.' end xiv• L. Walker is again assistant hon. secretary ittt,dit—ornea.3eB- George Vern-on and D. J. Price are the the f q form t "Mewing members, along with the officer., tyx•ecutive •.---N1 essrs U Box, W H Owen, D J Price, J H Singletol, C J Hayes, H Mercer, H L °r) T Knowles, J Brown, N McQuire, George P L Harrington, F Webster and T Mainwaring. HAROLD MERCER, before vacating the chair, thaiented Mr. W. G. Hayes, with a gold watch and 1441:n from the members, m a token of esteem and elation of the valuable services he has rendered to is,44vartch as secretary from its formation in 1906. A both bl,l3.Present was Mao handed to him for Mrs. llayes, )4 R"la I sing Suitably acknowledged by Hr. Hayes. IltirlMercer, on completing his year of office, was tbd with a chairman's badge and elected as hon. President of the branch.</p>
