        <p>Bequests to Employes. The will of the late Mr. John Geddes, J P., ef Warrington, and of Waverton, Cheshire, tea and, coffee merchant, chairman of the Longford Wire,lrcn, and Steel Company, has been proved at £37,500. Ile' left £lOO to John Gillies, 150 to Ernest Joe Andrews/ £25 to Fred Mann, £2O each to Arthur Greenough, John Andrews, and James Newell, £lO each to David Lewis and Joseph Booth—respectively in the service' of his firm at his deceaee, £3 to each other employe' over the age of 16 years, and £1 to each other employe under the age of 16 years. • IN MEMORIAM. Tn ever loving memory of my dear mother liessAll OWEN, who fell asleep January 17th,1897, aged 70 years. "Gone but not forgotten."</p>
